    "Observe the unchanged pinned DING constructor replacing its own previous workspace-specific instance; do not launch a substitute icon manager.",
    "Use held process identities, start times, XRes resources and private bus PID binding despite supporting-window XID reuse.",
    "Preserve the complete crash/startup outage and apply the unchanged temporal/pixel oracles to a separately declared recovered interval.",
    "Run full native input only after live recovery gates pass, bound to the new shell and DING lifetimes.",
    "Calibrate omitted reattachment independently from successful native recovery; omitted restart cannot pass from surviving pixels.",
    "Retain original mapped hashes while recognizing only the exact owned Mesa shader-cache index as mutable data; preserve the initial erroneous verifier rejection.",
    "Keep ordinary single-shell/lifetime checks, all existing native regressions and the original Show Desktop focus failure."
